adjudication.rationale:
In `deleteScheduledEmailReminder`, the `immediateDelete` branch (new signature) posts a SendGrid cancel request and then `return`s without updating or deleting the `WorkflowReminder` row (`cancelled` is not set, and no `delete`/`update` occurs). This is visible in the diff:
```ts
if (immediateDelete) {
  await client.request({ ... status: "cancel" ... });
  return;
}
```
Thus the DB can retain a reminder row that still appears scheduled/active (no `cancelled` flag, no delete), matching the finding.

In `scheduleEmailReminders.ts`, the new cancellation logic wraps the entire loop in a single `try/catch`:
```ts
try {
  const workflowRemindersToDelete = [];
  for (const reminder of remindersToCancel) {
    await client.request(...); // cancel in SendGrid
    workflowRemindersToDelete.push(prisma.workflowReminder.delete(...));
  }
  await Promise.all(workflowRemindersToDelete);
} catch (error) { ... }
```
If any `client.request` throws, control jumps to `catch`, aborting cancellation for remaining reminders and also skipping `await Promise.all(...)`, meaning previously queued Prisma deletes are never executed/awaited. This can cause the same cancelled reminders to be retried (and fail) on subsequent runs.
